  "question": "A random variable X takes values 1, 2, 3 with probabilities $k, 2k, 3k$ respectively. Find k. Also, find the mean and variance of X.",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "Sum of probabilities = 1<br />$k + 2k + 3k = 1$<br />$6k=1 \\implies k=\\frac{1}{6}$<br /><br />So, $P(1) = \\frac{1}{6}$, $P(2) = \\frac{2}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}$, $P(3) = \\frac{3}{6}=\\frac{1}{2}$<br /><br />Mean $=\\mu=E(X)=1\\times \\frac{1}{6}+2\\times\\frac{1}{3}+3\\times\\frac{1}{2}$<br />$=\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{3}{2}$<br />$=\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{4}{6}+\\frac{9}{6}=\\frac{14}{6}=\\frac{7}{3}$<br /><br />$E(X^2)=1^2\\times\\frac{1}{6}+2^2\\times\\frac{1}{3}+3^2\\times\\frac{1}{2}$<br />$=\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{9}{2}$<br />$=\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{8}{6}+\\frac{27}{6}=\\frac{36}{6}=6$<br /><br />Variance $=E(X^2)-(E(X))^2=6-(7/3)^2=6-\\frac{49}{9}=\\frac{54-49}{9}=\\frac{5}{9}$",
